(5024460, 732116, 52750, '<td valign="top">What I like most about this photo is the honesty. Being poor doesn''t equate to messy-haired kids with dirt smudged on their faces as too many photos in this category try to portray.</td>', 'What I like most about this photo is the honesty. Being poor doesn''t equate to messy-haired kids with dirt smudged on their faces as too many photos in this category try to portray.', '2008-10-25 11:26:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5024470, 732751, 52750, '<td valign="top">I feel bad for her... she''d be much warmer if she plugged that heater in. :(<br/> <br/>She has a great expression, the rain on the window helps with the gloomy feel of desperation. If I had to reshoot this, I think the unplugged heater makes the image look staged. And if there''s going to be a shadow on the wall, maybe including the light source in the pic would help (like a cheap lamp with no shade for example). Personally, I think getting in closer and using only the natural light from the window to illuminate her right side would have made this a very powerful shot. Let the rest fall to shadows. Just something to consider.</td>', 'I feel bad for her... she''d be much warmer if she plugged that heater in. :( She has a great expression, the rain on the window helps with the gloomy feel of desperation. If I had to reshoot this, I think the unplugged heater makes the image look staged. And if there''s going to be a shadow on the wall, maybe including the light source in the pic would help (like a cheap lamp with no shade for example). Personally, I think getting in closer and using only the natural light from the window to illuminate her right side would have made this a very powerful shot. Let the rest fall to shadows. Just something to consider.', '2008-10-25 11:38:03.000000', NULL, 1),
